---
import Layout from "../astro/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="About — dejpeg">
  <article style="padding:var(--space-4);max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      dejpeg is a browser-based JPEG artifact remover. It runs our
      custom-trained DeJPEGNet models entirely in your browser via WebGPU or
      WebAssembly, depending on what your device supports. Your images never
      leave your computer.
    </p>
    <p>
      The image is split into tiles, processed one at a time, and reassembled
      with feathered blending so any image size works without running out of
      memory.
    </p>
    <p>
      DeJPEGNet v2 is the default and stays closest to the original. The
      Texture version adds a slider for natural-looking grain, which is
      synthetic and not recovered detail. DeJPEGNet v1 is a smaller download.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
